This looks like a SWE-bench-style task (Multi-SWE-bench or SWE-bench Java) on jackson-databind, issue #1... "USE_BASE_TYPE_AS_DEFAULT_IMPL", which was added in 2.10. The task is to add a new MapperFeature and wire it into the type resolver builder (StdTypeResolverBuilder.buildTypeDeserializer), so that the base type becomes the default impl when the feature is enabled and no defaultImpl is set.

The change is small, but the hidden tests probably check specific behaviors. The fix touches a few places: MapperFeature, StdTypeResolverBuilder, and possibly the handling of abstract base types. The upstream fix is roughly:

```java
if ((_defaultImpl == null) && config.isEnabled(MapperFeature.USE_BASE_TYPE_AS_DEFAULT_IMPL) && !baseType.isAbstract()) {
    defaultImpl = baseType;
}
```

An agent could plausibly reproduce this. The name "iSWE-openmodels" suggests an open-model agent, which probably solves Java tasks at a moderate rate. The feature name is given in the issue title, which helps. The tests would use `MapperFeature.USE_BASE_TYPE_AS_DEFAULT_IMPL`, so the agent must name it exactly, and the title provides that name. Edge cases, such as abstract types, could still cause failures.

I estimate about 0.4.

