This item looks like a SWE-bench-style task from jackson-databind (issue #1627-ish). The feature is `MapperFeature.USE_BASE_TYPE_AS_DEFAULT_IMPL`, added in 2.10.

Solving it requires changes in `MapperFeature` and in `StdTypeResolverBuilder.buildTypeDeserializer`. The builder has to check the feature and, when `defaultImpl` is not set, use the base type if it is concrete. The hidden tests are probably in `TestDefaultForObject` or a new test class.

The upstream implementation, in `StdTypeResolverBuilder.buildTypeDeserializer`, looks like this:

```java
JavaType defaultImpl = defineDefaultImpl(config, baseType);
```

and `defineDefaultImpl`:

```java
if (_defaultImpl == null) {
    if (config.isEnabled(MapperFeature.USE_BASE_TYPE_AS_DEFAULT_IMPL) && !baseType.isAbstract()) {
        defaultImpl = baseType;
    }
}
```

The change is small, but the agent has to find the right spot. It also has to guess the feature's exact name, and the issue title supplies that. The harness is an agent harness, and MiniMax M2.5 is a decent model. The risk is that the exact behavior differs from what the hidden tests expect, for example the handling of abstract types and whether the check applies in other builders. I'd put the chance of success at moderate to good.

