This looks like a jackson-databind issue (#4... around 2.17/2.18) about AnnotationIntrospectorPair merging name and namespace. The fix touches `AnnotationIntrospectorPair.findNameForSerialization`, `findNameForDeserialization`, and possibly `findPropertyNamespace`. It is a moderately tricky issue because the hidden tests probably check specific behavior.

In the actual fix (databind #4... "JsonProperty and equivalents should merge with AnnotationIntrospectorPair"), the change in the pair is something like:

```java
public PropertyName findNameForSerialization(Annotated a) {
    PropertyName n = _primary.findNameForSerialization(a);
    if (n == null) {
        n = _secondary.findNameForSerialization(a);
    } else if (n == PropertyName.USE_DEFAULT) {
        PropertyName n2 = _secondary.findNameForSerialization(a);
        if (n2 != null) n = n2;
    }
    return n;
}
```

The fix needed to merge when the primary has an empty name or namespace. The tests likely use a custom introspector pair with a simple setup. An agent could plausibly get this right, but the exact semantics are ambiguous (for example, whether the result is non-null when only the namespace is present), so the hidden tests may fail on subtle details.

I'd estimate about a 0.45 chance of success.

