This is a jackson-databind issue (#3626), likely from a SWE-bench-style benchmark such as Multi-SWE-bench. The fix modifies CoercionConfigs: when the target type is Locale (FromStringDeserializer.Std), the empty-string coercion should return TryConvert instead of AsNull.

The actual fix in 2.14 was in CoercionConfigs.findCoercion:

```java
if (inputShape == CoercionInputShape.EmptyString) {
    // Since coercion of scalar must be enabled (see check above), allow empty-string
    // coercions by default even without this setting
    if (baseScalar
            // Default for setting is false
            || config.isEnabled(DeserializationFeature.ACCEPT_EMPTY_STRING_AS_NULL_OBJECT)) {
        return CoercionAction.AsNull;
    }
